          "name": "Dead Line - cue extract (English)",
          "entry": {
            "kind": {
              "kind": "static",
              "text": "DEAD LINE\nSample cue extract - English translation\n\nCOPYRIGHT NOTICE: This extract of the stage play is copyrighted. It is not released under the ToskLight Community License.\n\nSource: \"The Contents of the Package\", pages 51-52 of the author-provided 2018 script.\nThis short extract is bundled as a realistic static text source for Media testing.\n\nMia has decided that she will accept neither the ID card nor the weapon. Still angry, she walks\npurposefully to the microwave, throws the ID card inside, and switches it on. In the same motion,\nshe moves toward the weapon and decisively places the box over it.\n\nTrying to distract herself, Mia plugs the stereo back in, opens her laptop, and starts playback.\nShe puts the laptop beside her on the couch. The computer selects a random playlist: Moritz's\nplaylist, with the piano version of \"Mad World\". Mia restores part of the shrine, finds the\nphotograph from the Semicolon scene, sits down with it, and begins to cry.\n\nA notification appears on the laptop. First, the music fades down until it remains only in the\nbackground; then a notification sound is heard. The notification is an SMS from Moritz.\n\nMESSAGE\nSorry I just left. How did your presentation go?\nSent: 7 September 2018 - delivery failed\n\nShortly afterwards the music rises again, but it now sounds distorted and city noise can be heard.\n\nMIA\n(shouts toward the audience)\n\nMia becomes more desperate. A second notification follows, this time from Peter.\n\nMESSAGE\nTHANK YOU for supervising my bachelor's thesis five years ago.\nWithout you I would never have ended up here!!!\n\nMIA\n(shouts again, quieter than before - more a tearful cry)\n\nMia makes herself smaller. The city noise increasingly overwhelms the music. A further\nnotification arrives, this time from a social network.\n\nMESSAGE\nManage estate - Kurt Pellmann named you as his contact for administering his estate.\nThis action is now required.\n\nMia tries to scream, but no sound comes out. She collapses to the floor. The music can no longer\nbe heard; city noise has completely displaced it. Mia curls up tighter and tighter. The city noise\nslowly becomes rising feedback, growing louder. The world in the window accelerates and disappears.\nThe light darkens and a spotlight isolates Mia on the floor.\n\nThe feedback stops abruptly. Everything is black except the spotlight; the window is black too.\nMia sits up mechanically, staring blankly. [REDACTED]\n\nBLACKOUT.\n\nMia exits.\n"
            },
